<title>USA: Xytronyx not in line with some AMEX rules.</title>
<headline>Xytronyx not in line with some AMEX rules.</headline>
<dateline>SAN DIEGO 1997-02-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Xytronyx Inc, which develops and commercializes medical products with a focus on cancer treatment, said it was not in compliance with certain listing requirements of the American Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>This was due to its record of financial losses, cash outflows, reduced shareholder's equity and impaired financial condition, the company said.</p>
<p>Xytronyx said it was in talks with the exchange about its condition but there were no assurances its listing would be continued.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
